-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lex_splices_err_space_string.pcpp - Lexical: a blank after a splice in a string

  Break step of lex_splices: a blank between a backslash and its newline
  inside a string still makes a splice, LX0201, a warning at the
  backslash: "a" + "b" still joins and the module builds. The marked line
  ends in the splice, so its marker is a block-comment marker.
  Its bytes are part of the test (see above): edit it with an editor
  that keeps them as they are.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_splices_err_space_string;

/*
  @@test
    kind build
  @@end
*/

begin
  println(/* // WARN LX0201@41 // */ "a\ 
b");
end.
